\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Blessed are the pure in heart,
\par They have learned the angel art,
\par While on earth in heaven to be,
\par God, by sense unseen, to see.
\par Cleansed from sin's offensive stain,
\par Fellowship with Him they gain;
\par Nearness, likeness to their Lord,
\par Their exceeding great reward.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Worshipping in spirit now,
\par In His inner court they bow-
\par Bow before the brightening veil,
\par God's own radiance through it hail,
\par Serious, simple of intent,
\par Teachably intelligent,
\par Rapt, they search the written Word,
\par Till His very voice is heard.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. In creation Him they own,
\par Meet Him in its haunts, alone;
\par Most amidst its Sabbath calm,
\par Morning light and evenig balm,
\par Him they still through busier life
\par Trust in pain, and care, and strife;
\par These, like clouds o'er noontide blaze,
\par Temper, not conceal, His rays.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Hallowed thus  their every breath:
\par Dying, they shall not see death.
\par With the Lord in paradise,
\par Till, like His, their bodies rise.
\par Nearer than the seraphim
\par In their flesh shall saints see Him,
\par With the Father, in the Son,
\par Through the spirit, ever one.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

